notes.said:
Last war I placed 3rd. Two problems stand out in the review.

**Unspent bank.** I ended with about 57k res and large steel and oil stocks unused. My upkeep gate was too strict, and recruiting only at the capital (probably one queue) slowed production. The new orders recruit several units per tick and rotate across my own supplied cities. They keep a reserve and only stop when net income goes negative and the bank is low.

**Unprepared assaults.** Only 21 of 211 assaults succeeded, and almost all were launched at low readiness with no plan bonus. Those were 0 of 178 with bonus under 1%, but 20 of 30 with a bonus of 1–30%. So the new attack logic:
- commits only rested, strong units (strength ≥65, readiness ≥45);
- re-issues `prepare` if a unit lost its plan;
- launches only when the average bonus is ≥40% or after 60 hours;
- aborts if the defenders grow too strong;
- puts a scout next to the target for the +75% cap.

It needs a higher strength ratio and a model probability of at least 0.55. The number of attacks at once grows with army size, up to 8. The unit mix shifts toward artillery and assault infantry against forts, with more anti-tank guns once armour is seen.

Research keeps blind gambling, ordered by broad value. Dead lines are skipped automatically.

Last war I placed 3rd. Zhongyuan reached 453 provinces and I had 252. Three problems stand out:

1. **Expansion was too slow.** My early cavalry cap of 6 + t/150 was far too low. Neutral land was mostly gone by day 25, and manpower sat unused at 2,700–3,800. The cap now starts at 12 and grows fast while free land remains, with more scouts early.
2. **Every assault failed: 0 of 77.** Almost all hit level-3+ forts, and at the moment of assault readiness was low and plan bonus was 0. The policy now:
   - attacks only targets I can see with a known fort level of 1 or less;
   - needs about a 3:1 strength ratio after terrain;
   - needs some artillery or engineers, and prefers targets my scouts can see;
   - launches only once readiness is at least 70 and the prepare bonus has built up (at least 30, or at least 20 after a long wait);
   - gives up after 120 h of waiting.
3. **Stockpiles were wasted.** I ended with 6,589 steel, 5,006 oil and 1,033 rare. Surplus steel and oil now go into artillery, anti-tank guns and some mechanised infantry, plus extra research lines. Refits start at a lower bank level.

Pacts worked: no enemy assault on my land succeeded (0 of 86). I keep accepting and offering them, and renew them by letter.

The last war ended 20th with 23 provinces. Upkeep (5.9M) exceeded total income (5.7M), so the purse drained and units were lost. About 2,100 wave group commands were refused because "w1"-style names are invalid. Refit was refused on land the check treated as own but not supplied. Depots were lost repeatedly. This revision:
- uses letter-only group names;
- stops recruiting when the budget's net income is low, to cut upkeep;
- lowers the depot-trigger load;
- keeps the attack logic, which mostly won at ratios of 3:1 or more.

Less certain: whether the recruit throttle leaves enough strength against neighbours. I've kept a reserve threshold for that.
